A '''support gem''', or '''support''', is a type of [[gem]] used to modify the stats and behaviours of compatible [[skill gem]]s that it is [[link]]ed to.

==Mechanics==
Instead of granting a specific [[skill]] like [[skill gem]]s do, support gems modify any compatible skill gem linked to the support, modifying its behaviours as well as applying a [[mana]] [[cost]] multiplier. Many support-skill gem combinations are invalid; for example, a {{il|Clarity}} skill gem linked with {{il|Added Fire Damage Support}} will remain unchanged. Please note that [[gem tag]]s '''do not''' determine the supportability.<ref name="ref1" />

Multiple skill gems may be linked to a single support gem, in which case the support will modify all supported skills. Multiple support gems may be linked to a skill gem, in which case the skill gem will be modified by all of the supports. However, if two copies of a given support gem are linked to the same skill, only the higher level gem will apply. If a [[body armour]] contains two copies of a skill gem linked to different sets of support gems, two separate versions of the skill will be available, each with their own modifications. This may be desirable if for instance one version has been modified for single target damage, while another has been modified for [[area of effect]] damage. Support Gems add an icon in the form of a coloured letter or symbol to any supported skills' icons on the [[Skill bar|Skill Bar]]. 

Support gems with a given gem tag (e.g. fire/minion) do not benefit from modifiers like {{c|mod|+1 to Level of all # (e.g. Fire/Minion) Skill Gems}}, as support gems are not skill gems.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/2875467/filter-account-type/staff</ref> This includes hybrid gems with both support and skill components, such as {{il|Impending Doom Support}}, as it has the name "support" in the item name as well as the [[:Category:Support (gem tag)|support gem tag]].

===Greater supports===
Some support gems are "Greater" versions of other support gems. The effects of greater support gems override those of their ordinary counterparts. This means that they cannot be used together to support the same skill; the greater support will always take precedence. For example, if {{il|Multiple Projectiles Support}} and {{il|Greater Multiple Projectiles Support}} are both linked to the same skill gem, that skill will only be supported by the greater support.

Some greater support gems also have the [[Exceptional support gem|Exceptional]] tag.

==Exceptional gems==
{{main|Exceptional gem}}

Exceptional gems are gems that are obtained from [[endgame]] encounters and bosses, unlocked after defeating [[the Incarnations]] during the quest {{ql|Threads of the Originator}} for the first time. Exceptional support gems cannot be purchased from a vendor and must be obtained through specific methods.

Most exceptional gems are support gems, with a few of them being active gems (i.e. [[Pact]] skills). They can be "Greater" variants of existing support gems, enhancing their effects in interesting ways, or may be completely unique support effects. If they are "Greater" versions, they are mutually exclusive with their regular counterparts and only the exceptional version will apply, if possible. Exceptional gems have a default maximum gem level of 3 and require significantly more [[experience]] to level up.

==Awakened support gems==
{{main|Awakened support gem}}

Awakened support gems are a sunsetted system of endgame support gems prior to the rework of exception support gems. They could originally be obtained from [[Maven]]-witnessed map bosses, [[Maven's Invitation]]s, and the Maven herself as a [[pinnacle boss]]. Currently, most of them are considered [[legacy]] items and can only be traded for in [[permanent league]]s, with the exception of awakened exceptional support gems listed above.

They are considered the same gem as their non-awakened counterparts. If a skill gem is simultaneously supported by an awakened support and its non-awakened counterpart, only the awakened support gem's effects will apply, if possible.

