==List of non-gem supports==
Some [[unique item]] causes skill gems socketed to the item to be supported by a support not available from support gems.

* [[Divine Blessing Support]] (from {{il|March of the Legion}})
* [[Earthbreaker Support]] (from {{il|Dawnstrider}})
* [[Crab Totem Support]] (from {{il|The Crustacean's Call}})

==Related unique items==
The following [[unique item]]s are related to support gems:
{{Drop enabled unique item table
|where = items.stat_text LIKE "%support%gem%" AND items.stat_text NOT LIKE "%supported%by%"
|large=1
|base_item=1
|level=1
|stat=1
}}

The following [[unique item]]s grant support gems to socketed [[skill gems]]:
{{Drop enabled unique item table
|where = items.stat_text LIKE "%supported%by%"
|large=1
|base_item=1
|level=1
|stat=1
}}

==Related passive skills==
===Masteries===
The following [[Passive Mastery|Masteries]] are related to support gems:
{{Query masteries|where=mastery_effects.stat_text_raw LIKE "%support%gem%"}}

===Tattoos and runegrafts===
{{Drop enabled item table
|tables = tattoos
|join = items._pageID = tattoos._pageID
|where = items.class_id="StackableCurrency"
  AND tattoos.target IS NOT NULL
  AND items.description LIKE "%support%gem%"
|large=1
|description=1
}}

==Version history==
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.28.0|
* Greater versions of Supports no longer work alongside their non-Greater version, in a similar way to how Awakened Supports did not work with the corresponding non-Awakened version of the Support. In the case both versions of a Support are socketed, the Greater one takes priority.
* Existing Supports affected by this change include: Multiple Projectiles and Greater Multiple Projectiles, Volley and Greater Volley, Spell Echo and Greater Spell Echo.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.23.0|
* A substantial amount of damage-dealing skills have had their quality stats buffed. In most cases they will be significantly more powerful than before, and also more interesting. Many supports have also received changes to their quality stats.
* Anomalous, Divergent and Phantasmal Quality Gems have been removed from the game. Existing alternate Quality Gems now have the base Quality effect found on the respective Gem.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.15.0d|
* Adjusted Cost and Reservation Multipliers for various Support Gems.
}}
{{Version history table row|2.3.0|
* All Support Gems now have Support as part of their name.
* When you hover over a socketed Support Gem, it now shows what Skill Gems it affects by making them glow. The same is true for Skill Gems showing what Support Gems affect them. This currently does not properly handle the case of Support Gems that change a Skill Gem so that it enables or disables other Support Gems.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.9.3|
* Changed the gem-support system so that only Support Gems in the same physical group as a Skill Gem connect to it. If you have two groups with the same skill, you get two bindable skills. This is done so that supports can be made more impactful and so that players can have multiple variations of the same skill in their build.
* Support gems now have a flat multiplier to the mana cost of the skill that does not go up exponentially as they level up. Much of their benefit is available at the first level of the gem, but higher levels offer improvements (for free) if you meet their requirements. Support gems are balanced such that only a few of them are needed to make a skill feel powerful.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.8.6|
* Skill and [[support gem]]s can now have [[quality]], like [[equipment]]. Each [[gem]] is affected by quality in a specific way - for example, additional [[damage]] or [[attack speed]]. Skill gems from [[quest reward]]s have zero quality.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.8.4|
* Raised [[attribute]] requirements on all support gems. Many gems will no longer be usable until you gain more attributes.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.8.1|
* Nerfed [[elemental]] damage support gems.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.7.1|
* Reduced requirements of most early levels of support gems.
}}
{{Version history table row|0.6.7|
* Introduced to the game. The first gem was {{il|Greater Multiple Projectiles Support|Multiple Projectiles Support}}.
}}
{{Version history table end}}

